<title>DENMARK: Denmark revises 1996 c/a surpus up to 12.3 bln Dkk.</title>
<headline>Denmark revises 1996 c/a surpus up to 12.3 bln Dkk.</headline>
<dateline>COPENHAGHEN 1997-04-23</dateline>
<text>
<p>Denmark's National Statistics Office said on Wednesday that it had revised its figures for the 1996 current account to a surplus of 12.3 billion crowns from a previously published 10.9 billion.  </p>
<p>The office also revised the 1995 total to a surplus of 10.2 billion crowns, from a previously published 9.4 billion. --Steve Weizman, Copenhagen newsroom +45 339659650</p>
